<title>NETHERLANDS: ING no comment on Czech bank buy reports.</title>
<headline>ING no comment on Czech bank buy reports.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch financial services group ING Groep NV on Wednesday said it would not comment on reports it is a front runner to buy a stake in Czech bank Investicni a Postovni Banka.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't comment on rumours,&quot; ING's manager of corporate communications Ruud Polet told Reuters.</p>
<p>Organisations named by the Czech media as being interested in the Czech state's 31.5 percent stake in IPB are ING, ABN AMRO and Japanese investment bank Nomura.</p>
<p>Earlier, ABN AMRO also declined to comment.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
